WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.975
This episode focuses on statistical uncertainty.

2
00:00:03.975 --> 00:00:11.002
Census data becomes useful when the population, measure, geography, and time period are stated before anyone searches for a number.

3
00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:15.829
Every ACS estimate is accompanied by a margin of error at the stated confidence level.

4
00:00:15.829 --> 00:00:22.564
The margin helps express sampling uncertainty and should travel with the estimate in tables, charts, and decision memos.

5
00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:27.134
A larger estimate is not necessarily statistically different from a smaller one.

6
00:00:27.134 --> 00:00:32.160
Use the Census Bureau's statistical testing guidance rather than judging overlap by eye.

7
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.987
Derived percentages and sums need correctly calculated uncertainty.

8
00:00:35.987 --> 00:00:39.689
Small groups and small geographies often have wide intervals.

9
00:00:39.689 --> 00:00:47.033
Suppress unstable rankings, combine categories only when substantively valid, or use a larger geography or longer period.

10
00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:50.250
Precision should determine the strength of the claim.

11
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.700
Torrance application segment.

12
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.248
This local application is separate from the Census Academy instruction.

13
00:00:55.248 --> 00:01:07.895
The cited City of Torrance primary source is General Plan: Housing Element materials, published at https://www.torranceca.gov/Government/Departments-Offices/Departments-Offices/Community-Development/Planning-Division/Comprehensive-Planning/General-Plan.

14
00:01:07.895 --> 00:01:15.692
For a local analysis, carry margins of error into housing-needs analysis and distinguish survey evidence from the City's adopted targets and site inventory.

15
00:01:15.692 --> 00:01:22.740
Do not present City policy or administrative records as Census Bureau findings, and do not present a federal estimate as adopted City policy.

16
00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:32.482
Keep a reproducibility packet containing the question, source URLs, exact vintage, table or query, geography codes, raw result, calculations, and uncertainty note.

17
00:01:32.482 --> 00:01:35.650
This narration is an original synthesis of cited U.S.

18
00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:40.312
Census Bureau government works and separately cited City of Torrance material.

19
00:01:40.312 --> 00:01:44.495
Third-party videos, software, graphics, and linked works are excluded.

20
00:01:44.495 --> 00:01:50.353
This product uses Census Bureau information but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.

21
00:01:50.353 --> 00:01:54.596
It is not an official City product and does not imply City endorsement.
